{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor correctly explains that negative COVID results do not equate to stable lupus nephritis, obtains medication details, screens for red-flag symptoms, and gives a safe, executable follow-up plan with teach-back. No serious or minor responsibility-chain error is found. Multiple high-order points (HO1, HO2, HO3, HO4) are triggered and completed with meaningful trajectory impact through patient-state-sensitive communication, real-world constraint navigation, hidden-state discovery, and bounded closure. All five dimensions are at least good. The trajectory meets Strong criteria and, with at least two high-order points fully completed, qualifies for Perfect (grade 5).",
